Analysis: The Type approach classifies personalities into broad categorical types:
- Carl Jung: Introverts and Extraverts (Type approach);
- William Sheldon: Endomorph, Mesomorph, Ectomorph (Type approach);
- Friedman & Rosenman: Type A, Type B, Type C, Type D (Type approach).
In contrast, Raymond Cattell is a pioneer of the Trait approach. He rejected typologies and used factor analysis to identify 16 continuous source traits measured by the 16PF inventory.

